sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor A as Client A
    actor B as Client B
    participant H as HTTP layer<br/>(stateless, concurrent)
    participant Q as Claim queue
    participant W as Writer loop<br/>(single, serialized)
    participant M as In-memory state<br/>free list · claimed · idem keys
    participant S3 as S3 bucket

    rect rgb(238,242,248)
    Note over W,S3: BOOT — runs once, before the server accepts traffic
    W->>S3: GET snapshot/<latest>.json
    S3-->>W: pool + claims as of seq N
    loop until a key is missing (no LIST)
        W->>S3: GET log/<seq+1>.json
        S3-->>W: batch, or 404 — head of the log
    end
    W->>S3: GET lease.json, then PUT if free or expired
    S3-->>W: lease held (advisory only)
    W->>M: rebuild free list, claimed map, idem map
    Note over W: seq = N+k — now serving
    end

    rect rgb(240,248,240)
    Note over A,S3: HOT PATH — two concurrent claims, one S3 write
    A->>H: POST /claim  (Idempotency-Key: k1)
    B->>H: POST /claim  (Idempotency-Key: k2)
    H->>Q: enqueue(k1) — awaits promise
    H->>Q: enqueue(k2) — awaits promise
    W->>Q: drain (window skipped when idle; up to maxBatch)
    Q-->>W: [k1, k2]

    loop for each request in batch
        W->>M: idem hit? → replay prior result
        W->>M: else takeNext() — O(1), in memory
        M-->>W: code
    end

    Note over W,S3: nothing is acked yet — codes are only "assigned"
    W->>S3: PUT log/000043.json  (If-None-Match: *)<br/>{seq, batchId, claims[]}
    end

    alt 200 — committed (the durability point)
        S3-->>W: 200 OK
        W->>M: apply batch, seq++
        W-->>H: resolve(k1→CODE-A, k2→CODE-B)
        H-->>A: 200 {code: CODE-A}
        H-->>B: 200 {code: CODE-B}

    else 412 — fenced by another writer
        S3-->>W: 412 PreconditionFailed
        Note over W: seq 43 already exists → a second<br/>writer is live. We are NOT authoritative.
        W-->>H: reject batch
        H-->>A: 503 Service Unavailable
        H-->>B: 503 Service Unavailable
        W->>W: halt process — never issue uncommitted codes

    else timeout / network error — AMBIGUOUS
        S3--xW: no response
        Note over W: did the PUT land? Unknown.<br/>Must not ack, must not blind-retry.
        W->>S3: GET log/000043.json
        alt 404 — never landed
            S3-->>W: NoSuchKey
            W->>S3: retry PUT same seq 43
        else 200, batchId matches ours
            S3-->>W: our own entry
            W->>M: apply, seq++ → ack clients normally
        else 200, different batchId
            S3-->>W: someone else's entry
            W->>W: fenced → halt
        end
    end

    rect rgb(250,246,236)
    Note over W,S3: BACKGROUND — every N commits
    W->>S3: PUT snapshot/000043.json (full state)
    W->>S3: DELETE log/ entries older than PRUNE_RETAIN
    Note over W: keeps recovery to a couple of GETs
    end
